INT. LOST PROPERTY OFFICE - NIGHT

Shelves of umbrellas. A single desk lamp.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
You've kept everything.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
Everything that's ever been left.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Even this?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
Especially that. It's a green glove.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
It's a woman's green glove. Left hand.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
Left on the 9:14 from Aldgate. March, I think.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
The day Lady Harcourt vanished.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
I don't read the papers.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
You wrote the date on the tag.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
I write the date on every tag.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
The ink is fresh.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
It's a fresh tag.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
You rewrote it.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
Tags fade, Inspector.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Not in a drawer.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
It wasn't in a drawer.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Where was it?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
In my coat pocket.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
For how long?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
Since the morning after.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Why?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
I wanted to give it back.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
To whom?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
To her.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Lady Harcourt was on that train.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
I know.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
You saw her.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
I was on that train.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
You never said.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
Nobody asked.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
I'm asking now.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
She sat opposite me. Green gloves. She was crying.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Why was she crying?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
She didn't say.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Did she say anything?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
She asked me what the time was.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
What time was it?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
9:31.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
And then?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
She got off at Whitechapel.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Alone?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
A man held the door for her.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Describe him.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
Tall. Grey coat. A scar on his chin.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
You remember a scar.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
I remember everything left behind.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Did he leave anything?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
A newspaper. A hat.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Where are they?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
Shelf C. Second row.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
You've had them all this time.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
They were never claimed.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Miss Volkov. Why come forward now?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
Because you finally asked the right question.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Which was?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
What was left behind.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
And what was?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
Her.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
I don't follow.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
She never reached the platform. She's in the lost property.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Miss Volkov--

MIRIAM VOLKOV
Locker nine. Behind the umbrellas. Key's on the hook.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
You're confessing.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
I'm returning.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Sit down.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
I'd rather stand. It's my office.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Not for much longer.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
No. That's the sad part.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Why did you do it?

MIRIAM VOLKOV
She asked what the time was. I told her it was too late.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
That's not a reason.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
It's the only one I have.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Take the key down.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
Gladly.

INSPECTOR TOMAS ECHEVERRIA
Slowly.

MIRIAM VOLKOV
I have always been slow, Inspector. It's why I never lose anything.
